# Development Host Build Notes

These notes describe the original `dev-01` development host setup used for the virtual network lab. They are retained as historical implementation notes and should be adapted before use in a new environment.

## Base System

Install Ubuntu 16.04 Server with OpenSSH Server enabled.

## System Packages

Install the development packages used by the lab tooling:

```sh
sudo apt-get install gdebi-core python3-dev python-dev libtool-bin libcurl4-openssl-dev libpcre3-dev libssh-dev libxml2-dev
sudo apt-get install libxslt1-dev libtool-bin cmake pkg-config xsltproc pip npm nodejs-legacy
```

## Python Virtual Environment Setup

Verify that `pip` is available:

```sh
pip list
```

Install `virtualenv`:

```sh
pip install virtualenv
virtualenv --version
```

Install `virtualenvwrapper`:

```sh
pip install virtualenvwrapper
source /usr/local/bin/virtualenvwrapper.sh
pip list | grep virtual
```

## Virtual Environment Locations

The original lab stored Python virtual environments under:

```text
/home/lab/.virtualenvs
```

Create the directory if it does not already exist:

```sh
mkdir -p ~/.virtualenvs
```

Set the `WORKON_HOME` variable:

```sh
export WORKON_HOME=~/.virtualenvs
```

Set the project directory. The original lab used:

```text
/home/lab/projects
```

```sh
mkdir -p ~/projects
export PROJECT_HOME=~/projects
```

Reload `virtualenvwrapper`:

```sh
source /usr/local/bin/virtualenvwrapper.sh
```

To make the settings persistent, add the following lines to `.bashrc`:

```sh
export WORKON_HOME=~/.virtualenvs
export PROJECT_HOME=~/projects
source /usr/local/bin/virtualenvwrapper.sh
```

## Common Virtualenvwrapper Commands

Enter a virtual environment:

```sh
workon myenv
```

List existing virtual environments:

```sh
lsvirtualenv
```

Exit a virtual environment:

```sh
deactivate
```

Remove a virtual environment:

```sh
rmvirtualenv myenv
```

Create an isolated virtual environment:

```sh
mktmpenv
```

Copy a virtual environment:

```sh
cpvirtualenv <source-env> <target-env>
```

List installed site packages from inside the active virtual environment:

```sh
lssitepackages
```

Remove third-party packages from the current virtual environment:

```sh
wipeenv
```

## Node.js Tooling

Verify that `npm` is available:

```sh
npm -v
```

Install the Node.js tools used by the original lab workflow:

```sh
sudo npm install bower -g
sudo npm install gulp -g
```

## Sanitization Note

The `/home/lab` paths are example values from the original lab. Replace them with paths that match your development host before using these notes in another environment.
